l,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Typically experienced during football game programming; event entry policies apply.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"ou-sooner-schooner-victory-ride","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Sooner Schooner victory ride","title":"See the Sooner Schooner Run","subtitle":"Owen Field after OU scores","notes":"Watch for the covered wagon and its white ponies after an OU score, and leave driving and animal handling to the designated spirit squads.","short_summary":"A covered wagon makes a score-following ride.","evidence_claim":"OU says the Sooner Schooner races across Owen Field after every OU score, pulled by matching white ponies named Boomer and Sooner.","source_url":"https://www.ou.edu/about/history","source_title":"History | The University of Oklahoma","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"View from authorized stadium seating or public event areas; do not approach the horses or wagon.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"ou-chant-one-finger","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"The OU Chant and raised finger","title":"Raise One Finger for the Chant","subtitle":"A unity gesture during “Oklahoma”","notes":"During the OU Chant, follow the documented gesture: stand and raise one finger, then join only if you know the words and setting.","short_summary":"The chant pairs lyrics with a raised-finger gesture.","evidence_claim":"OU states that students, student-athletes, alumni, and fans are encouraged to stand and raise one finger during the Chant as a symbol of unity.","source_url":"https://www.ou.edu/about/history","source_title":"History | The University of Oklahoma","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"A public school-spirit practice; follow the etiquette and instructions of the event.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"ou-boomer-sooner-yell","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"The Yell (“Boomer Sooner”)","title":"Learn the Original Yell","subtitle":"A chant adopted after OU’s first football season","notes":"Recognize the “Hi rickety whoop-te-do” lines as the university’s documented yell, not simply a generic fight-song refrain.","short_summary":"OU’s early football culture produced the “Boomer Sooner” yell.","evidence_claim":"OU says students formulated and adopted the yell in fall 1895 after the first football game and first oratorical contest made a yell necessary.","source_url":"https://www.ou.edu/about/history","source_title":"History | The University of Oklahoma","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"A public school-spirit practice; participate appropriately for the event.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"ou-pride-drum-major-strut","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Pride of Oklahoma Drum Major Strut","title":"Spot the Drum Major’s Strut","subtitle":"A distinctive Pride of Oklahoma movement","notes":"During a Pride performance, watch the drum major’s practiced back-bending field movement, formally known within the band as “the strut.”","short_summary":"The band’s drum major performs a named marching movement.","evidence_claim":"OU identifies the Pride of Oklahoma drum major’s distinctive game-day movement as “the strut” and describes it as a Sooner tradition.","source_url":"https://www.ou.edu/web/news_events/articles/news_2015/oupridelore","source_title":"7 Things You (Maybe) Don’t Know About the Pride of Oklahoma | The University of Oklahoma","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2015-08-31","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":n